{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "about": [
    "The key names hotkey values are written with, in every mod. See data/fixtures/canonical-ini/README.md for the binding syntax and scripts/generate-config-schema.mjs for what reads this file.",
    "name: the written spelling, which is Unity's KeyCode member name. Names read ASCII case-insensitively. aliases: other names Unity declares for the same value; they read as the key and are written as its name.",
    "vk: the Windows virtual-key code, only where the name and the code mean the same key on every keyboard layout. Codes with no name here (the VK_OEM_* punctuation keys among them) are written as hex, 0x01 to 0xFE, in native mods.",
    "unity: the UnityEngine.KeyCode value. Every member of the enum is here but None, Unity's value for no key, which is unity_unbound: an empty list is how a file says unbound.",
    "The Unity names and values were read off UnityEngine.KeyCode in the shipped assemblies of 18 games, Unity 5.3.4 to 6000.3.15, which agree on every value. unity_sources lists them by Steam folder name, with the engine version each ships."
  ],
